bin/R: parse arguments with parameter expansion, no sed, no bash

R.sh.in's argument loop ran `echo ... | sed` (three times per `R -e`).
The loop is replaced whole and uses POSIX parameter expansion, so
starting R runs no sed and needs no bash (configure-only.sh pins
R_SHELL=/bin/sh); `echo` is gone from the -e/-f path too, because
dash's echo rewrites backslashes. Cases other than the sed ones are
upstream's, except that `R CMD` runs Rcmd with /bin/sh rather than a
PATH lookup of `sh`. SED stays exported for rtags and javareconf, as a
bare name found on PATH. feat-no-host-paths PLAN.md, phase A3.

